# Modelfile for qwen25-classify — the A.R.C.H.I.E. coordinator-lane model.
#
# The coordinator lane routes dispatch's lightweight meta-reasoning
# (classify / sentiment / tagging / detect_language) to this one designated,
# always-warm, GPU-free small model. See platform_v2/services/coordinator_lane.py
# and .claude/plans/2026-07-06-coordinator-lane-design.md.
#
# Provenance (verified on the live hub Ollama, 2026-07-07):
#   qwen25-classify shares the EXACT qwen2.5:1.5b weights blob
#   (sha256-183715c435899236895da3869489cc30ac241476b4971a20285b1a462818a5b4,
#   986 MB). It is qwen2.5:1.5b re-created with a CPU pin (num_gpu 0) + a fixed
#   2048-token context. Captured via `ollama show qwen25-classify --modelfile`
#   and rewritten with a portable `FROM qwen2.5:1.5b` (the live model's FROM is
#   a raw blob path, which is NOT reproducible off-hub — this is).
#
# The CPU pin (num_gpu 0) is a coordinator-lane invariant: the model must stay
# small + GPU-free so hub admission control never sheds it (it is classified as
# non-GPU-class in model_sizes + _SMALL_MODEL_MARKERS).
#
# Rebuild on any node that already has qwen2.5:1.5b:
#   ollama create qwen25-classify -f Modelfile.qwen25-classify
#
# TEMPLATE + LICENSE are inherited from qwen2.5:1.5b automatically.
FROM qwen2.5:1.5b
SYSTEM """You are Qwen, created by Alibaba Cloud. You are a helpful assistant."""
PARAMETER num_ctx 2048
PARAMETER num_gpu 0
